As at 28-8-2926:

JavaScript Directory (/js/)
ai.js: Adaptive learning module that tracks move success rates and records turn outcome history for AI adaptation.

combat.js: Core combat engine managing the turn resolution loop, move priorities, damage formulas, Chi/Faint accumulation, and KO/Victory triggers.

common.js: Shared helper utilities, math routines, and global state helpers used across multiple scripts.

cpu_controller.js: AI decision-making controller that evaluates available moves according to selected difficulty levels (Easy, Normal, Hard).

foresee_engine.js: Predictive calculation engine that evaluates potential move outcomes and counter-play options for AI decision-making.

game.js: Main game orchestrator and entry point initializing global application states, game modes, and event hooks.

item.js: Logic handler for managing item usage, inventory effects, and combat consumables.

media.js: Video controller managing video preloading, iOS mobile video playback unlocking, center screen transitions, and directional sprite flipping (scaleX).

simulator.js: Headless combat simulation engine used to run rapid, asynchronous CPU vs. CPU matches for win-rate and balance analytics.

storage.js: Persistence manager handling localStorage reads and writes for saved AI knowledge, match stats, and user preferences.

ui.js: DOM UI renderer managing HUD stat updates, health bars, damage popups, and status indicators.

vs_select.js: Character selection screen controller managing Rider selection states, difficulty toggles, and match setup parameters.

CSS Directory (/css/)
style.css: Master stylesheet defining layouts, HUD overlays, video scaling containers, battle animations, control pad styling, and visual themes.

Data Directory (/data/)
items.js: Data dictionary defining available items, their attributes, costs, and in-game effects.

moves.json: Move set database defining move commands, type classifications, Chi costs, base damage, hit chances, buff parameters, and video file associations for each Kamen Rider.

riders.json: Character roster registry storing base stats (LP, Archetype), asset paths, finisher display names, initial orientation (sourceFacing), and active/unlock flags.
